<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:camunda="http://camunda.org/schema/1.0/bpmn" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:modeler="http://camunda.org/schema/modeler/1.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="Definitions_userOnboarding" targetNamespace="http://example.com/bpmn" modeler:executionPlatform="Camunda Platform" modeler:executionPlatformVersion="7.24.0">
  <bpmn:error id="Error_onb_404" name="User not found" errorCode="HTTP_404" />
  <!--
    Start variables:
      apiBaseUrl   e.g. http://localhost:8081/api   (the nginx mock)
      userId       1042
      userChanges  JSON object 2 (partial user)
      contactA / contactB  objects merged + flattened into the contact body
      initiator, deleteReason (optional)
  -->
  <bpmn:process id="user-onboarding" name="User onboarding" isExecutable="true" camunda:historyTimeToLive="P30D">
    <bpmn:startEvent id="onbStart" name="Onboarding requested">
      <bpmn:outgoing>o1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="onbGetUser" name="GET user" camunda:delegateExpression="${restGet}">
      <bpmn:documentation>[REST connector] REST GET - Fetch data: request params built from the pasted OpenAPI parameters; 4xx -&gt; BPMN error HTTP_&lt;status&gt;.
Implementation: delegateExpression ${restGet}
Inputs (leave empty when not needed):
- url: Request URL. Supports ${expressions} and {placeholders} that are filled from params with "x-in": "path". Example: ${apiBaseUrl}/users/{userId}
- sources: Comma separated process variable names (or a JSON literal) deep-merged in order - later wins. Example: currentUser, userChanges
- paramsSchema: Paste the operation's "parameters" list from the service's OpenAPI / Swagger document (in: path | query | header). A parameter is filled from the merged sources, else from the process variable with the same name. Paste it as JSON or YAML (OpenAPI 3.x or Swagger 2.0); "$ref"s must resolve inside the pasted text, so paste the referenced components too, or the whole document plus a top-level "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Name". Add "x-source": "/json/pointer" or "x-expression": "varName" (no dollar-brace wrapper) where your process data is named differently. Long pastes (a whole OpenAPI document) work with history level activity or none; with audit / full history the engine stores every input in history and limits it to 4000 characters.
- headers: JSON object, values may use ${expressions}. Example: {"X-Correlation-Id": "${execution.processInstanceId}"}
- responseSchema: Optional. Paste the response schema from the service's OpenAPI / Swagger document: a schema object, a response, or the operation's "responses" (the first 2xx is used). Shapes the response (only declared properties are kept, writeOnly ones dropped) and validates it. Violation -&gt; BPMN error RESPONSE_INVALID. Paste it as JSON or YAML (OpenAPI 3.x or Swagger 2.0); "$ref"s must resolve inside the pasted text, so paste the referenced components too, or the whole document plus a top-level "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Name". Add "x-source": "/json/pointer" or "x-expression": "varName" (no dollar-brace wrapper) where your process data is named differently. Long pastes (a whole OpenAPI document) work with history level activity or none; with audit / full history the engine stores every input in history and limits it to 4000 characters.
- resultVariable: Process variable receiving the response body (stored as JSON).
- statusVariable: Process variable receiving the HTTP status code.
- technicalErrors: exception (default): the task fails - incident, or retried with async before. bpmnError: thrown as BPMN error HTTP_5xx / CONNECTION_FAILED so an error boundary event or error event subprocess can handle it. 4xx (HTTP_4xx) and schema errors (REQUEST_INVALID / RESPONSE_INVALID) are always BPMN errors.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <camunda:inputOutput>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="url">${apiBaseUrl}/users/{userId}</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="sources">userChanges</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="paramsSchema">{
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["userId", "X-Tenant"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "userId": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "x-in": "path", "x-expression": "userId"},
    "fields": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {"type": "string", "enum": ["contact", "preferences", "roles"]},
      "uniqueItems": true,
      "x-in": "query",
      "default": ["contact", "preferences"]
    },
    "filter": {
      "type": "object",
      "x-in": "query",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "theme": {"type": "string", "x-source": "/user/preferences/theme"},
        "phone": {"type": "string", "x-source": "/user/contact/phone"}
      }
    },
    "X-Tenant": {"type": "string", "x-in": "header", "default": "acme"}
  }
}</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="headers" />
          <camunda:inputParameter name="responseSchema">{
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["user"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {"user": {"$ref": "#/$defs/user"}},
  "$defs": {
    "user": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["id", "name"],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "id": {"type": "integer"},
        "name": {"type": "string"},
        "contact": {"type": "object"},
        "preferences": {"type": "object"},
        "roles": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}
      }
    }
  }
}</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="resultVariable">currentUser</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="statusVariable" />
          <camunda:inputParameter name="technicalErrors">bpmnError</camunda:inputParameter>
        </camunda:inputOutput>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>o1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>o2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:boundaryEvent id="onbNotFound" attachedToRef="onbGetUser">
      <bpmn:outgoing>o404</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:errorEventDefinition errorRef="Error_onb_404" />
    </bpmn:boundaryEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="onbPutUser" name="PUT merged user" camunda:delegateExpression="${restPut}">
      <bpmn:documentation>[REST connector] REST PUT - Replace a resource: body built from merged sources + pasted OpenAPI schema.
Implementation: delegateExpression ${restPut}
Inputs (leave empty when not needed):
- url: Request URL. Supports ${expressions} and {placeholders} that are filled from params with "x-in": "path". Example: ${apiBaseUrl}/users/{userId}
- sources: Comma separated process variable names (or a JSON literal) deep-merged in order - later wins. Example: currentUser, userChanges
- paramsSchema: Paste the operation's "parameters" list from the service's OpenAPI / Swagger document (in: path | query | header). A parameter is filled from the merged sources, else from the process variable with the same name. Paste it as JSON or YAML (OpenAPI 3.x or Swagger 2.0); "$ref"s must resolve inside the pasted text, so paste the referenced components too, or the whole document plus a top-level "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Name". Add "x-source": "/json/pointer" or "x-expression": "varName" (no dollar-brace wrapper) where your process data is named differently. Long pastes (a whole OpenAPI document) work with history level activity or none; with audit / full history the engine stores every input in history and limits it to 4000 characters.
- bodySchema: Paste the request schema from the service's OpenAPI / Swagger document: a schema object (components.schemas.X), the requestBody, or the whole operation. Builds + validates the body from the merged sources; only declared properties are sent, readOnly ones are left out. Empty = send the merged sources as-is. Paste it as JSON or YAML (OpenAPI 3.x or Swagger 2.0); "$ref"s must resolve inside the pasted text, so paste the referenced components too, or the whole document plus a top-level "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Name". Add "x-source": "/json/pointer" or "x-expression": "varName" (no dollar-brace wrapper) where your process data is named differently. Long pastes (a whole OpenAPI document) work with history level activity or none; with audit / full history the engine stores every input in history and limits it to 4000 characters.
- headers: JSON object, values may use ${expressions}. Example: {"X-Correlation-Id": "${execution.processInstanceId}"}
- responseSchema: Optional. Paste the response schema from the service's OpenAPI / Swagger document: a schema object, a response, or the operation's "responses" (the first 2xx is used). Shapes the response (only declared properties are kept, writeOnly ones dropped) and validates it. Violation -&gt; BPMN error RESPONSE_INVALID. Paste it as JSON or YAML (OpenAPI 3.x or Swagger 2.0); "$ref"s must resolve inside the pasted text, so paste the referenced components too, or the whole document plus a top-level "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Name". Add "x-source": "/json/pointer" or "x-expression": "varName" (no dollar-brace wrapper) where your process data is named differently. Long pastes (a whole OpenAPI document) work with history level activity or none; with audit / full history the engine stores every input in history and limits it to 4000 characters.
- resultVariable: Process variable receiving the response body (stored as JSON).
- statusVariable: Process variable receiving the HTTP status code.
- technicalErrors: exception (default): the task fails - incident, or retried with async before. bpmnError: thrown as BPMN error HTTP_5xx / CONNECTION_FAILED so an error boundary event or error event subprocess can handle it. 4xx (HTTP_4xx) and schema errors (REQUEST_INVALID / RESPONSE_INVALID) are always BPMN errors.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <camunda:inputOutput>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="url">${apiBaseUrl}/users/{userId}</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="sources">currentUser, userChanges</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="paramsSchema">{
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["userId"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {"userId": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "x-in": "path", "x-source": "/user/id"}}
}</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="bodySchema">{
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["user"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "user": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["id", "name", "contact", "preferences"],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "id": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1},
        "name": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1},
        "contact": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["email", "phone"],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "email": {"type": "string", "format": "email"},
            "phone": {"type": "string", "minLength": 5}
          }
        },
        "preferences": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["theme", "notifications"],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "theme": {"type": "string", "enum": ["light", "dark", "system"]},
            "notifications": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": ["email", "sms"],
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "email": {"type": "boolean"},
                "sms": {"type": "boolean"},
                "push": {"type": "boolean"}
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "roles": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "uniqueItems": true}
      }
    }
  }
}</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="headers" />
          <camunda:inputParameter name="responseSchema" />
          <camunda:inputParameter name="resultVariable">updatedUser</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="statusVariable">putStatus</camunda:inputParameter>
          <camunda:inputParameter name="technicalErrors">bpmnError</camunda:inputParameter>
        </camunda:inputOutput>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>o2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>o3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="onbPatchPreferences" name="UPDATE preferences" camunda:delegateExpression="${restUpdate}">
      <bpmn:documentation>[REST connector] REST UPDATE (PATCH) - Partially update a resource: body built from merged sources + pasted OpenAPI schema.
Implementation: delegateExpression ${restUpdate}
Inputs (leave empty when not needed):
- url: Request URL. Supports ${expressions} and {placeholders} that are filled from params with "x-in": "path". Example: ${apiBaseUrl}/users/{userId}
- sources: Comma separated process variable names (or a JSON literal) deep-merged in order - later wins. Example: currentUser, userChanges
- paramsSchema: Paste the operation's "parameters" list from the service's OpenAPI / Swagger document (in: path | query | header). A parameter is filled from the merged sources, else from the process variable with the same name. Paste it as JSON or YAML (OpenAPI 3.x or Swagger 2.0); "$ref"s must resolve inside the pasted text, so paste the referenced components too, or the whole document plus a top-level "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Name". Add "x-source": "/json/pointer" or "x-expression": "varName" (no dollar-brace wrapper) where your process data is named differently. Long pastes (a whole OpenAPI document) work with history level activity or none; with audit / full history the engine stores every input in history and limits it to 4000 characters.
