- headers: JSON object, values may use ${expressions}. Example: {"X-Correlation-Id": "${execution.processInstanceId}"}
- responseSchema: Optional. Paste the response schema from the service's OpenAPI / Swagger document: a schema object, a response, or the operation's "responses" (the first 2xx is used). Shapes the response (only declared properties are kept, writeOnly ones dropped) and validates it. Violation -&gt; BPMN error RESPONSE_INVALID. Paste it as JSON or YAML (OpenAPI 3.x or Swagger 2.0); "$ref"s must resolve inside the pasted text, so paste the referenced components too, or the whole document plus a top-level "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Name". Add "x-source": "/json/pointer" or "x-expression": "varName" (no dollar-brace wrapper) where your process data is named differently. Long pastes (a whole OpenAPI document) work with history level activity or none; with audit / full history the engine stores every input in history and limits it to 4000 characters.
